{"id":"3dac77f5-5060-4113-a48c-fc53532a69b6","zed":"context","version":"0.4.0","text":"\n\n\n```html next-bound-frontend/src/app/shared/components/navbar/navbar.component.html\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <p-menubar [model]=\"items\">\n    <ng-template pTemplate=\"start\">\n      <div class=\"flex align-items-center gap-2\">\n        <img\n          src=\"nbicon.png\"\n          style=\"height: 30px; width: 30px\"\n          alt=\"logo\"\n          class=\"w-8\"\n        />\n        <h1 class=\"text-lg\">NextBound</h1>\n      </div>\n    </ng-template>\n    <ng-template pTemplate=\"item\" let-item let-root=\"root\">\n      <a pRipple class=\"flex align-items-center p-menuitem-link\">\n        <span [class]=\"item.icon\"></span>\n        <span class=\"ml-2\">{{ item.label }}</span>\n        <p-badge\n          *ngIf=\"item.badge\"\n          [ngClass]=\"{ 'ml-auto': !root, 'ml-2': root }\"\n          [value]=\"item.badge\"\n        />\n        <span\n          *ngIf=\"item.shortcut\"\n          class=\"ml-auto border-1 surface-border border-round surface-100 text-xs p-1\"\n          >{{ item.shortcut }}</span\n        >\n        <i\n          *ngIf=\"item.items\"\n          [ngClass]=\"[\n            'pi',\n            root ? 'pi-angle-down ml-2' : 'pi-angle-right ml-auto',\n          ]\"\n        ></i>\n      </a>\n    </ng-template>\n    <ng-template pTemplate=\"end\">\n      <div class=\"flex align-items-center gap-2\">\n        <input\n          type=\"text\"\n          pInputText\n          placeholder=\"Search\"\n          class=\"w-8rem sm:w-auto\"\n        />\n        <p-avatar\n          image=\"https://primefaces.org/cdn/primeng/images/demo/avatar/amyelsner.png\"\n          shape=\"circle\"\n        />\n      </div>\n    </ng-template>\n  </p-menubar>\n</div>\n```\n\nActualemnte, lo que contiene el pTemplate=\"end\" es un input y un avatar, que deberia estar a la derecha del menubar, pero no se ve asi\nPara asegurarte de que el contenido del `pTemplate=\"end\"` (el input y el avatar) se alinee a la derecha del menubar, puedes agregar algunas clases de estilo adicionales para forzar la alineación correcta. En este caso, puedes usar clases de flexbox para alinear los elementos correctamente.\n\nAquí hay una versión modificada de tu código HTML con las clases de estilo adicionales:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <p-menubar [model]=\"items\" class=\"flex justify-content-between\">\n    <ng-template pTemplate=\"start\">\n      <div class=\"flex align-items-center gap-2\">\n        <img\n          src=\"nbicon.png\"\n          style=\"height: 30px; width: 30px\"\n          alt=\"logo\"\n          class=\"w-8\"\n        />\n        <h1 class=\"text-lg\">NextBound</h1>\n      </div>\n    </ng-template>\n    <ng-template pTemplate=\"item\" let-item let-root=\"root\">\n      <a pRipple class=\"flex align-items-center p-menuitem-link\">\n        <span [class]=\"item.icon\"></span>\n        <span class=\"ml-2\">{{ item.label }}</span>\n        <p-badge\n          *ngIf=\"item.badge\"\n          [ngClass]=\"{ 'ml-auto': !root, 'ml-2': root }\"\n          [value]=\"item.badge\"\n        />\n        <span\n          *ngIf=\"item.shortcut\"\n          class=\"ml-auto border-1 surface-border border-round surface-100 text-xs p-1\"\n          >{{ item.shortcut }}</span\n        >\n        <i\n          *ngIf=\"item.items\"\n          [ngClass]=\"[\n            'pi',\n            root ? 'pi-angle-down ml-2' : 'pi-angle-right ml-auto',\n          ]\"\n        ></i>\n      </a>\n    </ng-template>\n    <ng-template pTemplate=\"end\">\n      <div class=\"flex align-items-center gap-2 ml-auto\">\n        <input\n          type=\"text\"\n          pInputText\n          placeholder=\"Search\"\n          class=\"w-8rem sm:w-auto\"\n        />\n        <p-avatar\n          image=\"https://primefaces.org/cdn/primeng/images/demo/avatar/amyelsner.png\"\n          shape=\"circle\"\n        />\n      </div>\n    </ng-template>\n  </p-menubar>\n</div>\n```\n\nEn este código, he añadido la clase `ml-auto` al `div` dentro del `pTemplate=\"end\"`. Esto debería forzar que el contenido se alinee a la derecha del menubar. Además, he añadido la clase `flex justify-content-between` al `p-menubar` para asegurar que los elementos dentro del menubar se distribuyan correctamente entre el inicio y el final.\n","messages":[{"id":{"replica_id":0,"value":0},"start":0,"metadata":{"role":"user","status":"Done","timestamp":{"replica_id":0,"value":60}}},{"id":{"replica_id":0,"value":51},"start":1737,"metadata":{"role":"assistant","status":"Done","timestamp":{"replica_id":0,"value":61}}},{"id":{"replica_id":0,"value":52},"start":4036,"metadata":{"role":"user","status":"Done","timestamp":{"replica_id":0,"value":62}}}],"summary":"Menubar End Template Issue","slash_command_output_sections":[{"range":{"start":0,"end":1},"icon":"Library","label":"Default","metadata":null},{"range":{"start":3,"end":1601},"icon":"File","label":"next-bound-frontend/src/app/shared/components/navbar/navbar.component.html","metadata":{"path":"next-bound-frontend/src/app/shared/components/navbar/navbar.component.html"}}]}